    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-162310",
      "knowledge_point_id": "0c2c755c-59e0-5048-b20c-507f13fce441",
      "knowledge_point": "Geometric Interpretation of the Roots of Unity",
      "problem": "Which of the following diagrams shows all the $8$th roots of unity?",
      "worked_solution": "Geometrically, the $8$th roots of unity have the following properties:\n\n- all of them lie on the unit circle centered in the origin,\n\n- one of the roots is $1,$ corresponding to the point $(1,0)$ on the complex plane,\n\n- the roots form a regular octagon (regular $8$-sided polygon).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980994/assets/51ac4ad5bbc626c58ddbb6efd8c06bb665ef0849591dd846dd959756ea6e41b6.png)",
